.TH MD_GET_TEXT 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.2.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_get_text \- copy a channel message snapshot as a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

int md_get_text(const morsedec_decoder_t *decoder, uint64_t id, char
    *buffer, size_t capacity, size_t *required);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copy a channel message snapshot as a string.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Decoder handle. Calls using this handle must be serialized, including queries.
.TP
.I id
Stable channel ID, or zero for the current channel.
.TP
.I buffer
Caller-owned destination. NULL is allowed only when capacity is zero.
.TP
.I capacity
Destination capacity in bytes, including room for the terminating NUL.
.TP
.I required
Non-NULL output address for the required byte count, including the terminating
NUL.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns MORSEDEC_SUCCESS (1) on success, or MORSEDEC_FAILURE (0) and sets
errno on failure. Do not inspect errno after success.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
NULL decoder or required, or NULL buffer with nonzero capacity.
.TP
.B ENOENT
Nonzero id does not identify a tracked channel.
.TP
.B ENOSPC
Destination is too small; *required includes the NUL byte.
.SH REMARKS
Copies each character byte and word_end spaces, followed by NUL. The encoding
is Latin-1, not UTF-8. Prosigns retain their lowercase pair representation;
undecodable runs may appear as an asterisk. The copied string belongs to the
caller. It is a full revisable snapshot, not newly decoded text.
.PP
Call with buffer=NULL and capacity=0 to query the size. Keep the handle
serialized across a size query and the corresponding copy, or retry if a later
call reports ENOSPC. If id=0 and no current channel exists, the empty string
requires one byte. A fixed buffer of 3*MORSEDEC_MESSAGE_CAPACITY+1 bytes
covers the present character-plus-two-spaces maximum.
.PP
On ENOSPC, *required is updated and no string bytes are written; there is no
truncation or partial string. On other failures the output values are not
specified. Reading text does not consume or clear it. Copy pending text after
each processing call and once after md_flush().
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize all calls that access the same handle, including getters. Different
handles may process concurrently after construction. These functions are not
specified as async-signal-safe.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0 (shared-library ABI
1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_get_characters (3),
.BR md_get_channel (3),
.BR md_flush (3)
